$$
x \le z - 1,\ y \le z - 1,\ \text{and}\ z > \max(x, y)
$$

This means:

$$
x, y \in \{1, 2, \dots, z - 1\}
$$

So for each $z$, we can consider how many pairs of $x, y$ come from the set $\{1, 2, \dots, z-1\}$.

